<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Sea Harvest raises yr attrib profit 17 pct.</title>
<headline>Sea Harvest raises yr attrib profit 17 pct.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Sept 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)    57.1	  vs   49.1</p>
<p>    Shr, headline (cts)  54.7	  vs   48.9</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		17.0 making 26.0 vs 23.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   57.58	 vs  49.09</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   98.37	 vs  88.12</p>
<p>    Tax			 38.07	 vs  39.04</p>
<p>    Net investment income 14.04	 vs  12.68</p>
<p>    Turnover		 418.46	 vs 360.92</p>
<p>Div payable Jan 7</p>
<p>on register Dec 6</p>
<p>Full name: Sea Harvest Corp Ltd</p>
<p>    Share of associates'  2.73 loss   vs  -</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said good winter catches and favourable trading conditions during the second half, supported by improved operating efficiencies and a lower tax rate, lifted attributable earnings 17 percent.</p>
<p>It said that good progress was made in reducing the average age of the fleet with the acquisition of three modern stern trawlers.</p>
<p>Sea Harvest said that it anticipated the markets in which it operates to remain firm in the coming financial year. Providing catch rates in South Africa and Namibia are satisfactory and the group's present quotas are maintained, real growth in earnings could be expected, it added.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
